// Wait for the dpkg/apt lock instead of failing immediately.
//
// This is defensive, not a fix for an observed failure: the post-deploy
// failure that prompted it turned out to be /run/lock/usg.lock contention
// between parallel BOSH post-deploy scripts, not dpkg contention (see the
// LOCK CONTENTION note in jobs/harden/templates/bin/post-deploy).
//
// It is still worth having. This job's post-deploy runs several apt
// operations and then `usg fix`, whose package_* rule remediations invoke apt
// internally. Concurrent apt activity -- apt-daily.service /
// apt-daily-upgrade.service, unattended-upgrades, or Ubuntu Pro client work
// from the sibling ubuntu-advantage-pro-token job's pre-start -- holds
// /var/lib/dpkg/lock-frontend and makes apt exit non-zero straight away.
// Waiting is the correct behaviour for an unattended deploy, and this config
// is the only way to influence the apt calls made inside `usg fix`, which we
// cannot pass flags to.
DPkg::Lock::Timeout "600";
